/**

@page page_exahype_faq FAQ and troubleshooting

# The space-time predictor diverged

An ADER-DG solver without a limiter ends the run when the Picard iteration of
a cell diverges, and prints the time stamp, the centre of the first diverged
cell and the number of diverged cells on the rank. A solver with a subcell
limiter marks the cell as troubled and recomputes it with the finite-volume
scheme. Reduce the time step factor or add a limiter.

# The simulation is unstable

An adaptive solver ends the run with a non-critical assertion when its time
step size drops to 1e-10 or below and writes the last solution. The message
states the maximum eigenvalue that leads to this time step size. Check the PDE
terms, the initial condition and the boundary conditions. An ADER-DG solver
needs a subcell limiter for a solution with shocks.

# The maximum eigenvalue is not finite

An adaptive solver ends the run with a non-critical assertion when a cell
reports an infinite or negative wave speed and writes the last solution. The
plotted snapshot shows the cell; check the initial condition and the
boundary conditions of that cell.

# The solver memory grows in segments

A pool reserves whole segments of slots. The reported solver memory rises in
steps of one segment per pool when the grid grows. It stays when the grid
shrinks until every slot of the last segment is free.

*/
